#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "522b66f4-8a46-5dd0-a9d7-3b081c0ed157" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Point and a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2ce03c34-8e2c-5554-a129-1eaf05ad46fd" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-12548" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(3,2)$ and the line $x=5$." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/526/Source/Images/075ce483c7effa23b544c4e110e41b82.png)\n\nSince the line $x = 5$ is vertical, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(3,2)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between $x$-coordinate of the point and $5$.\n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd = \\mid 3 - 5 \\mid = 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7030a12-bd18-5f8b-84eb-28b6f216f972" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Point and a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "64a6782b-aa64-5027-8311-3498c19c39e1" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-12549" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(1,3)$ and the line $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x -5$." :question/worked-solution "Let's draw a diagram describing our situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/526/Source/Images/20c50cfc96d069b4dd030c77c6959b60.png)\n\nFirst, we find the equation of the line that is perpendicular to\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{2}x - 5\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(1,3)$.\n\nThe given line has a slope of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nso our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-2$.\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 3 &= -2(x - 1) \\\\\ny - 3 &= -2x + 2 \\\\\ny &= -2x + 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{y = \\frac{1}{2}x - 5; y =-2x + 5\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by setting the two equations equal and solving for $x$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}x - 5 &= -2x + 5 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2}x + 2x &= 5 + 5 \\\\\n\\frac{5}{2}x &= 10 \\\\\nx &= 10 \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\\nx &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-3$. So, our solution is $x=4$ and $y=-3$. Consequently, the lines intersect at the point\n\n$$\n\\left(4,-3\\right)\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(1,3)$ and\n\n$$\n\\left(4, -3 \\right)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\sqrt{(x_{2} - x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} - y_{1})^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4 - 1)^{2} + (-3 - 3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 36} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{45} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9}\\sqrt{5} \\\\\n&= 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(1,3)$ and the line\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{2}x -5\n$$\n\nis $3 \\sqrt{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Line That Is Closest to a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "57fc631b-c251-55d2-a9d5-6b41fc4bb00c" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-12612" :question/problem "Find the point on the line $y-x=4$ that is closest to the point $(3,3)$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/526/Source/Images/8d76b170141a85d09dbefe8efdfd59dd.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the equation of the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - x &= 4 \\\\\ny &= x + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the equation of the line that is perpendicular to\n\n$$\ny = x + 4\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(3,3)$.\n\nThe given line has a slope of $1$, so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-1$.\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 3 &= -1(x - 3) \\\\\ny - 3 &= -x + 3 \\\\\ny &= -x + 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{y = x + 4; y =-x + 6\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 4 &= -x + 6 \\\\\nx + x &= 6 - 4 \\\\\n2x &= 2 \\\\\nx &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ into either of the two equations gives $y=5$. So, our solution is $x=1$ and $y=5$. Consequently, the lines intersect at the point $(1,5)$.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the point on the line $y-x= 4$ that is closest to the point $(3,3)$ is $(1,5)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "522b66f4-8a46-5dd0-a9d7-3b081c0ed157" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Point and a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb14a9b8-35bd-5a1c-9812-1f4cf955d28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073239} {:answer/id #uuid "c17f492b-7afb-50ef-8a00-e263933db541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073240} {:answer/id #uuid "f096e959-0c07-5c05-9065-fcacdef3c5fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073241} {:answer/id #uuid "029c4470-7187-5688-9ee5-b5e57a676e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073242} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3eceb3-8cd6-566f-847c-b1cc5490d072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "029c4470-7187-5688-9ee5-b5e57a676e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073242} :answer-field/id #uuid "9889c593-708f-5999-b96a-7b15dd26891c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073238}] :question/id #uuid "119ea192-657f-5438-a868-40ca8f32ea19" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-74034" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(5,-1)$ and the line $y = 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074457 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Line That Is Closest to a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8f7c7d4-e70c-5d4d-baea-be96141ede63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073257} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce16184-f1a2-5896-8704-c49d339e0b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, \\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073258} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0133ec-cc00-5cf7-a3a8-b1516648c07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073259} {:answer/id #uuid "67e8903b-94f3-50fa-babc-f0a1bb48e7f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{9}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073260} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7314e9-9ff0-5c31-8ec2-c7fa22c053ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b0133ec-cc00-5cf7-a3a8-b1516648c07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073259} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc7b8bce-af09-5f2d-8ae9-c03b3a21bdbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073256}] :question/id #uuid "a2a5b92a-6d2c-561b-999b-9dedaf72311f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-74060" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/526/Source/Images/q-74060.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $2y - 3x = 3$ that is closest to the point $(2,-2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Line That Is Closest to a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2bfd806-d96d-56ef-8a17-050382fa91aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073263} {:answer/id #uuid "fede7757-e7a0-5856-9c97-41f31a5a1d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{9}{2}, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073264} {:answer/id #uuid "03a06aec-2288-5d72-b3a4-d001f55825e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073265} {:answer/id #uuid "07ad4d9b-7194-5406-b69d-0c0180c2b050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073266} {:answer/id #uuid "229299ff-0b09-522d-a797-aba1addf9b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "229299ff-0b09-522d-a797-aba1addf9b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073267} :answer-field/id #uuid "e56869ec-9da3-5d01-a62d-b1a42d38a26c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073262}] :question/id #uuid "853cfa3c-da08-562e-b7e9-24b69cddbfcd" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-74061" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/526/Source/Images/q-74061.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $y =-\\frac{2}{3}x - 2$ that is closest to the point $(2, 1)$."}]}
